				"⠁⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				138,
				2
			],
			"Message": "chore(Land): Update Element submodules and fix formatter path\n\nSynchronize the Element git submodule to the latest revision (7d937e8d) to incorporate build configuration standardization and IPC stability improvements across the editor ecosystem. The update includes:\n\n- **Mountain & Echo:** Standardize service entry points to the universal `Fn` convention and fix `Mountain` ↔ `Cocoon` IPC to prevent null dereferences when handling `sky:model:contentChanged` events for non-existent documents.\n- **Cocoon, Wind, Worker, & Output:** Normalize ESBuild configurations (indentation, export syntax) and re-align 100+ compiled artifacts to ensure correct module evaluation order.\n\nAdditionally, update `Maintain/Format.sh` to reference the `.prettierignore` file with a relative path (`--ignore-path \".prettierignore\"`) instead of the absolute root variable, ensuring the formatter script functions correctly when invoked from subdirectories.\n\nNo functional logic is altered; changes are focused on build pipeline robustness, type safety, and code consistency.",
			"SHA": "7ba697e2e174ae58f42a9ee5c6d5ae70309aacae"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-05-23T02:24:20Z",
			"File": [
				"⠁⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				138,
				2
			],
			"Message": "chore(Land): Extend formatter exclusions for Wind generated types\n\nUpdate `.prettierignore` and `biome.json` to exclude auto-generated BridgeShape type definitions produced by the Wind UI service layer. These files reside in `Element/Wind/Source/Effect/*/Implementation/` and carry the `Generated` suffix, mirroring the exclusion patterns for upstream VS Code schemas.\n\nThis prevents linter and formatter overhead on immutable build artifacts while ensuring consistency with the existing exclusion strategy for `gen/` and `Configuration/` output directories.",
			"SHA": "ae6287679133100ae8453bbcf892d21ac070337f"
		},
